   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Organization for Migration (IOM)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustaining the Expansion of the Overseas Health Assessment and Management of U.S.-Bound Refugees, Non-immigrant Visa Applicants and Other Migrant Populations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The link between human mobility and health is high on the global health agenda since the recent COVID-19 pandemic. IOM has been implementing a &apos;Global Health Security Partnership Engagement; Public health and epidemic preparedness&apos; project&amp;nbsp;through the technical and financial support by the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) of the United States since 2021. The proposed project is a continuation of border health activities and implementation in collaboration with the respective Ministries of Public Health (MoPH) in Central Asian project, Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC), Jordan and Lebanon. The project comprised several activities, such as needs assessments at Points of Entry (PoE), Training of Trainers (ToT) and cascade training on responding to health emergencies at the border, institutionalization of the training materials in the relevant educational institutions, and the development of Standard Operational Plans (SOPs).</narrative>
  </description>
